\author{utensil}
\date{2026-10-16}

\p{Finite incidence data carry fields, difference operators and
observables. What remains of a theory when some field values are
eliminated, and which changes of background preserve the resulting
observables? An [alternating four-cycle](fdip-0003) supplies a common
example whose maps, normalization factors and comparison failures can
be computed exactly.}

\p{[Ring-valued fields and operator products](fdip-0015) lead to
[paired differences](fdip-0016), then
[real Gaussian states](fdip-0017) and
[retained observables](fdip-0018).
[Background symmetries](fdip-0019) and
[group-algebra sectors](fdip-001A) organize these constructions.
[Configuration Clifford algebras](fdip-001B) and
[spatial Dirac operators](fdip-001C) are distinct realizations,
followed by [arithmetic families](fdip-001D) and
[enriched background comparisons](fdip-001E).}

\p{These finite results test a broader conjecture relating discrete
induction, arithmetic geometry, Clifford sheaves, background moduli and
special L-values. A continuum limit, a moduli-stack construction and a
physical identification of L-values remain separate questions.
Recovering Standard Model or gravitational equations requires explicit
constructions and comparisons of observables; the finite identities
below do not establish those identifications.}

